#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: docvariables.docbook:12 docvariables.docbook:43 docvariables.docbook:197
#: docvariables.docbook:337 docvariables.docbook:386 docvariables.docbook:426
#: docvariables.docbook:432 docvariables.docbook:446 docvariables.docbook:462
#: docvariables.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: docvariables.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "introduction"
msgstr "introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A variable is a simple way of allowing &kword; to modify the document in "
"<emphasis>very</emphasis> specific ways to reflect the changing nature of "
"the document or report."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A variable can be a number (such as a page number, the total number of pages "
"in a document, etc), a selection of words (clients name, product name, the "
"documents filename, etc), a date, a time, or nearly anything you desire."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the variable is defined, a <emphasis>placeholder</emphasis> is inserted "
"in the document. &kword; will replace this placeholder with the value of "
"that variable each time the placeholder is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Variables can either be <emphasis>fixed</emphasis> (which means that once "
"inserted, their value does not change), or <emphasis>variable</emphasis> "
"(where the placeholder is <link linkend=\"update-variables\">updated by "
"&kword;</link> to reflect the current value of the variable)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter will begin with a few examples of commonly used variables "
"(<link linkend=\"insert-date\">date</link>, <link linkend=\"insert-time"
"\">time</link>, and <link linkend=\"page-number\">page numbers</link>), then "
"detail the <link linkend=\"misc-variable\">remaining variables</link> "
"available to you. Finally, it will detail how to <link linkend=\"custom-"
"variables\">create custom variables</link> for documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "Date and Time"
msgstr "Data e ora"

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many letters, reports and documents contain information about the dates or "
"times they correspond to. The date and time information may establish the "
"creation of a document (which will remain fixed as long as the document is "
"around), or the date and time may serve as a notice of the last date of "
"modification (which would change with each passing day)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; allows for both fixed and variable date and time variables in the "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert Date"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: docvariables.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "<secondary>insert date</secondary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: docvariables.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>insert date</primary>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert the date in the document, simply place the cursor in the text box "
"where the date should be inserted and select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Variable</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Date</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. This will bring up several selections. To "
"insert the current date, select one of two options: <guimenuitem>Current "
"date (fixed)</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Current date (variable)</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: docvariables.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Current date (fixed)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting this option will insert the current date into the current cursor "
"position. This date is determined by checking with the computers system "
"clock. Once entered, this value will not change, even when &kword; is asked "
"to <link linkend=\"update-variables\">update the document variables</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This item is ideal for dates of document creation, or when including data in "
"a report from todays work. Compare this choice to <guimenuitem>Current date "
"(variable)</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: docvariables.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Current date (variable)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting this option will insert the current date into the current cursor "
"position. This date is determined by checking with the computers system "
"clock. This value will change when &kword; is asked to <link linkend="
"\"update-variables\">update the document variables</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option is good for any point in the document where the current date is "
"always wanted. Compare this choice to <guimenuitem>Current date (fixed)</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once the date has been selected, a dialog box will appear."
