#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: docvariables.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "custom"
msgstr "personalizat"

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has many predefined variables. You may encounter documents where it "
"would be nice to define your own variables for a document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using <emphasis>Custom Variables</emphasis>, you can create an unlimited "
"number of variables for each document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a new custom variable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: docvariables.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "create custom variable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new custom variable, place the cursor at the location in the "
"document to insert the new variable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guisubmenu>Variable</"
"guisubmenu><guisubmenu>Custom</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. This will bring up a dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the variable name and its current value in the text boxes provided."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to create the new variable name and insert "
"it at the current cursor location. Click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to "
"cancel the creation of the new variable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is now possible to <link linkend=\"insert-custom-variables\">insert this "
"new variable</link> at any place in your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit a custom variables value"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: docvariables.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid "edit custom variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order for variables to be useful, you need to be able to give them a "
"value, and be able to change that value easily. To change the value of a "
"variable:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Custom Variables..."
"</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. This will bring up a dialog "
"box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each custom variable has a line in this table. The first column is the name "
"of the variable, and the second column is the value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the value of a variables, simply click within the text box to the "
"right of the variable name. Enter the desired value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When all the changes have been complete, simply click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> and all the variables will be updated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert a custom variable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: docvariables.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid "insert custom variable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert a new custom variable select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Variable</guisubmenu><guisubmenu>Custom</guisubmenu> </"
"menuchoice> from the menubar. The custom variable is listed in the submenu. "
"Click on the name of the variable and &kword; will insert the variable, with "
"its current value, at the cursor location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "Updating All Variable Values"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: docvariables.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "updating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can tell &kword; to update all variable values (to make sure all "
"variables are set to their current values). This is <emphasis>especially</"
"emphasis> important with dates and times."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guisubmenu>Variable</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Refresh All Variables</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> "
"from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docvariables.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Updating One Date or Time Variable Value"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can tell &kword; to update a single date or time variable value, and "
"leave the others unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docvariables.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply place the mouse pointer over the variable you want to update and "
"click with the &RMB;. Select <guimenuitem>Change Variable To</guimenuitem>. "
"A small menu will appear which will show several new date or time formatting "
"options and the option to change either dates or times to fixed or variable "
"time formats. Simply select the new option and this variable will be updated."
msgstr ""

